{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.AlphaEmHabiroBarInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.AlphaEmHabiroBarInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution.lean#L65-L71","doc":"**Special value `H(ζ_2) = H(−1) = −2`** (the bar / charge-\nconjugation mode). At `q = qi = −1`: `[2]_q = −2`, `h = 0`, so\n`H = −2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution.lean#L58-L63","doc":"**Special value `H(ζ_1) = H(1) = 2`** (the classical leading term\ngiving `α/(4π)`). At `q = qi = 1`: `[2]_q = 2`, `h = 0`, so `H = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution.lean#L48-L56","doc":"**Bar-involution fixed point.** `H` is invariant under the bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹` (swapping `q ↔ qi`):\n`H(qi, q, α) = H(q, qi, α)`. The proof is pure `ring` — the swap fixes\n`q + qi` and squares away the sign in `(q − qi)²`. This is the\nfibre-level (formal-variable) statement; no reality is used. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution","label":"prop:alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaEmHabiro","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/alpha-em-habiro-bar-involution.lean#L40-L46","doc":"The α_EM **Habiro element** `H = [2]_q · (1 − h²·α)` written with\n`q` and its inverse `qi` as independent variables (subject to\n`q · qi = 1` where that identity is needed). `[2]_q = q + qi`,\n`h = q − qi`, so `H = (q + qi)·(1 − (q − qi)²·α)`. Generic `CommRing`:\nno reality, no archimedean evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}